---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology — Is Poland Safe Now?"
  description="How Is Poland Safe Now? classifies regional security status using TypeSafe AI, and the limits of the current pipeline."
  path="/methodology"
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Methodology</h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Current phase: live, news-grounded classification</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Every region's status is produced by <code>TypeSafeAiClassificationService</code>, which first collects
        recent headlines from Polish and international news portals (covering roughly the last 48 hours), then
        sends them to TypeSafe AI's System One API to classify each of the 16 voivodeships from that evidence. The
        collection itself is not persisted or scheduled yet (see <a class="underline" href="/about">About</a>) — it
        runs fresh on each request, cached briefly to avoid refetching on every page load. If a region has no
        relevant headline, or the TypeSafe AI call is unavailable, misconfigured, or returns something unusable,
        that region shows <strong>Unknown</strong> — never a false Green.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Status levels</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Green</strong> — no elevated regional signal found.</li>
        <li><strong>Yellow</strong> — elevated situation requiring attention.</li>
        <li><strong>Red</strong> — serious active warning or confirmed incident.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Unknown</strong> — missing, stale, conflicting, or insufficient information. Missing data always
          resolves to Unknown, never Green.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Planned pipeline (not yet implemented)</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        A future phase will persist collected news and classifications to the database with full evidence trails,
        re-run on a schedule via a Cron Trigger instead of on-demand per request, and broaden collection beyond
        RSS search queries — following the same <code>ClassificationService</code> interface this phase already
        defines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Map data</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Voivodeship boundaries are sourced from Poland's official geospatial registry (GUGiK PRG) and converted to a
        local SVG at development time — see
        <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/pvgomes/ispolandsafenow/blob/main/DATA_SOURCES.md">
          DATA_SOURCES.md
        </a>
        in the repository for the full attribution and license.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Limits</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This is an independent information service, not an official warning system, and cannot guarantee safety.
        Always follow instructions from Polish authorities and RCB. For emergencies, call 112.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
